            <ArticleTitle>[A man with abdominal pain and subsequently a periumbilical haematoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1468</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 71-year-old male presented with periumbilical ecchymosis formed after acute onset of abdominal pain and near collapse. At the time of presentation the haematoma was the only symptom. Following a CT scan, the diagnosis of a contained rupture of an iliac artery aneurysm was made. The patient was successfully treated with an endovascular stent graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
